Sommelier: the Info.plist built into the Wine loader marks every program it runs as a game, so macOS Game Mode can
engage for a game that runs from inside its shortcut app (gamepolicyd labels the process from the category it
finds in the executable's Info.plist; without a category it ignores Wine processes). Programs started outside a
shortcut app (Steam, launchers) stay "BackgroundOnly" in Launch Services and aren't affected. The app adds the same
keys to engines built before this patch (SommelierKit's LoaderGameLabel).

--- a/loader/wine_info.plist.in
+++ b/loader/wine_info.plist.in
@@ -25,6 +25,10 @@
     <key>NSPrincipalClass</key>
     <string>WineApplication</string>
     <key>LSUIElement</key>
     <string>1</string>
+    <key>LSApplicationCategoryType</key>
+    <string>public.app-category.games</string>
+    <key>LSSupportsGameMode</key>
+    <true/>
 </dict>
 </plist>
